"Some keyboard layouts (such as AZERTY) require a modifier to press a number key. This causes problems for switching to a window, tab, or split pane by pressing modifier+number: you might need other modifiers or conflicting modifiers. When “Emulate US Keyboard” is enabled, you can press the configured modifier plus the key on the top row that corresponds to a number key on a US keyboard. For example, on AZERTY, the & key would act as the 1 key." = "某些鍵盤佈局（如 AZERTY）需要修飾鍵才能按下數字鍵。這會導致透過按修飾鍵+數字來切換視窗、分頁或分割窗格時發生問題：您可能需要其他修飾鍵或存在衝突的修飾鍵。啟用「模擬 US 鍵盤」後，您可以按配置的修飾鍵加上頂行中對應 US 鍵盤數字鍵的按鍵。例如，在 AZERTY 佈局上，& 鍵將充當 1 鍵。";
"The leader behaves like a modifier key, such as Command or Option, but is a separate keystroke. It can be used in key bindings. For example, if you set the leader to ⌘b then you could bind an action to the two-keystroke sequence “⌘b x”. ⌘b is the recommended leader and that keystroke will not be used for other purposes in the future." = "Leader 鍵的作用類似修飾鍵（如 Command 或 Option），但它是一個獨立的按鍵。它可用於鍵綁定。例如，如果您將 Leader 設為 ⌘b，則可以將操作綁定到雙鍵序列「⌘b x」。⌘b 是推薦的 Leader 鍵，該按鍵未來不會用於其他用途。";
